    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Question\n\nHello! \r\nWhen I use [mini.diff](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.diff) and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?\r\nI would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.\r\n\r\nI use lazyvim with [my config](https://github.com/jmarcelomb/nvim) on top.\r\n\r\nThank you!!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.diff</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!<br>\nWhen I use <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.diff\">mini.diff</a> and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?<br>\nI would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I use lazyvim with <a href=\"https://github.com/jmarcelomb/nvim\">my config</a> on top.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you!!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.diff\nQuestion\nHello!\nWhen I use mini.diff and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?\nI would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.\nI use lazyvim with my config on top.\nThank you!!",
