            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\n> When I use [mini.diff](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.diff) and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?\r\n\r\nI am afraid, this is not possible and out of scope for 'mini.diff'. Its overlay text is implemented via virtual text which is not meant for \"go inside of it\".\r\n\r\n> I would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.\r\n\r\n*That* is partially possible via [this mapping](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-diff.html#minidiff.operator). \"Partially\" - because the whole reference text of the hunk will be yanked (copied).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I use <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.diff\">mini.diff</a> and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, this is not possible and out of scope for 'mini.diff'. Its overlay text is implemented via virtual text which is not meant for \"go inside of it\".</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>That</em> is partially possible via <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-diff.html#minidiff.operator\" rel=\"nofollow\">this mapping</a>. \"Partially\" - because the whole reference text of the hunk will be yanked (copied).</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi!\n\nWhen I use mini.diff and I toggle the overlay, I would like to be able to go into the hunks to be able to copy from them, how can I do this?\n\nI am afraid, this is not possible and out of scope for 'mini.diff'. Its overlay text is implemented via virtual text which is not meant for \"go inside of it\".\n\nI would like to be able to select and copy virtual text, I guess.\n\nThat is partially possible via this mapping. \"Partially\" - because the whole reference text of the hunk will be yanked (copied).",
